{:edb/db-before-t 2458 :edb/db-after-t 2459 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535771 50 #inst "2026-10-09T06:52:35.893Z" 13194139535771 true] [17592186133790 1020 #edb/ref 17592186365404 13194139535771 true] [17592186133792 1020 #edb/ref 17592186365411 13194139535771 true] [17592186134359 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535771 true] [17592186134359 1100 "Let $V = C[- π, π]$ be the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[- π, π]$, equipped with the inner product\n$⟨f(t), g(t)⟩ = ∫_{- π}^{π}f(t)g(t)dt$.\nGiven the functions $f(t) = t$ and $g(t) = \\sin t$, which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $⟨f(t), g(t)⟩ = 2π$\n2. $⟨f(t), g(t)⟩ = 0$\n3. $f(t)⊥g(t)$ with respect to the inner product $⟨ \\cdot, \\cdot ⟩$ in $V$" 13194139535771 false] [17592186134359 1100 "Let $V=C[-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ be the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[-\\pi ,\\pi ],$ equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n⟨f(t),g(t)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(t)g(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nGiven the functions $f(t)=t$ and $g(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $⟨f(t),g(t)⟩=2\\pi $\n- $⟨f(t),g(t)⟩=0$\n- $f(t)⊥g(t)$ with respect to the inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ in $V$" 13194139535771 true] [17592186134359 1145 "First, we need to evaluate \n\n$$\n⟨f(t),g(t)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nLet's use integration by parts. We denote\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=t & ⟹ & {u}^{′}=1, \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & ⟹ & v=\\int {v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}t=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, applying the integration by parts formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t & =uv{|}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }-{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{u}^{′}v\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t){|}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }+{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(-\\pi \\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi -\\pi \\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\pi ))+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t{|}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi } \\\\  & =(\\pi +\\pi )+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\pi )) \\\\  & =2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's now examine the statements:\n\n- Statement I is true, while statement II is false. This is as a result of the above calculations.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since the inner product is not zero, our vectors are not orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139535771 true] [17592186365404 1017 #edb/ref 17592186365405 13194139535771 true] [17592186365404 1089 "q-97442" 13194139535771 true] [17592186365404 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535771 true] [17592186365404 1100 "Let $V=C[0,1]$ be the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[0,1],$ equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{1}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nIf $x(t)={t}^{2}$ and $y(t)=k+3t$ are orthogonal with respect to the inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ in $V,$ then $k=$" 13194139535771 true] [17592186365404 1113 #uuid "f480f100-1995-590a-9540-47ba0d705389" 13194139535771 true] [17592186365404 1145 "Since $x(t)$ and $y(t)$ are orthogonal, their inner product must be zero.\n\nFirst, we compute the inner product using our definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x(t),y(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{t}^{2}(k+3t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(k{t}^{2}+3{t}^{3})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(\\frac{k{t}^{3}}{3}+\\frac{3{t}^{4}}{4}){|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{3}+\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set $⟨x(t),y(t)⟩=0$ and solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x(t),y(t)⟩ & =0 \\\\ \\frac{k}{3}+\\frac{3}{4} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{k}{3} & =-\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ k & =-\\frac{9}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535771 true] [17592186365405 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365406 13194139535771 true] [17592186365405 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365407 13194139535771 true] [17592186365405 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365408 13194139535771 true] [17592186365405 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365409 13194139535771 true] [17592186365405 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365410 13194139535771 true] [17592186365405 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535771 true] [17592186365405 1041 "selection" 13194139535771 true] [17592186365405 1104 #edb/ref 17592186365408 13194139535771 true] [17592186365405 1110 #uuid "9996d238-92a3-5041-9c02-4500350bce67" 13194139535771 true] [17592186365406 1034 "-\\frac{3}{4}" 13194139535771 true] [17592186365406 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535771 true] [17592186365406 1111 #uuid "8729dedd-99f4-5bd4-b822-9e3fc8513768" 13194139535771 true] [17592186365407 1034 "\\frac{8}{3}" 13194139535771 true] [17592186365407 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535771 true] [17592186365407 1111 #uuid "b3843d0b-1803-56e8-b32f-af509f5da38c" 13194139535771 true] [17592186365408 1034 "-\\frac{9}{4}" 13194139535771 true] [17592186365408 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535771 true] [17592186365408 1111 #uuid "56b94ba8-213a-5261-b334-5d564abf8093" 13194139535771 true] [17592186365409 1034 "\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139535771 true] [17592186365409 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535771 true] [17592186365409 1111 #uuid "a57ad915-f413-5d09-976d-1c9c48ce9bb8" 13194139535771 true] [17592186365410 1034 "-\\frac{4}{3}" 13194139535771 true] [17592186365410 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535771 true] [17592186365410 1111 #uuid "a0ec3745-68e9-534c-8ee2-76a55a591e92" 13194139535771 true] [17592186365411 1017 #edb/ref 17592186365412 13194139535771 true] [17592186365411 1089 "q-97449" 13194139535771 true] [17592186365411 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535771 true] [17592186365411 1100 "Let $V=C[0,\\pi ]$ be the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[0,\\pi ],$ equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n⟨f(t),g(t)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }f(t)g(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nGiven the functions $f(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)$ and $g(t)=1,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $⟨f(t),g(t)⟩=\\pi $\n- $⟨f(t),g(t)⟩=0$\n- $f(t)⊥g(t)$ with respect to the inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ in $V$" 13194139535771 true] [17592186365411 1113 #uuid "5a53cb6e-220d-5e52-afd0-69dc504c17a4" 13194139535771 true] [17592186365411 1145 "We need to evaluate\n\n$$\n⟨f(t),g(t)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe can evaluate this integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={[-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)}{2}|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\pi )}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡0}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's now examine the statements:\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. This is as a result of the above calculations.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since the inner product is zero, our vectors must be orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" 13194139535771 true] [17592186365412 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365413 13194139535771 true] [17592186365412 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365414 13194139535771 true] [17592186365412 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365415 13194139535771 true] [17592186365412 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365416 13194139535771 true] [17592186365412 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365417 13194139535771 true] [17592186365412 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535771 true] [17592186365412 1041 "selection" 13194139535771 true] [17592186365412 1104 #edb/ref 17592186365413 13194139535771 true] [17592186365412 1110 #uuid "22410652-8ca7-54b5-bf18-bca90f903a5e" 13194139535771 true] [17592186365413 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535771 true] [17592186365413 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535771 true] [17592186365413 1111 #uuid "afab6836-6d21-527f-b92e-e76b0474653c" 13194139535771 true] [17592186365414 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535771 true] [17592186365414 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535771 true] [17592186365414 1111 #uuid "14319543-aa0d-53f3-8b4c-be797169d621" 13194139535771 true]